INTERPRETATION
At K=2Q+3 the odd quotient is JN_2.  The analyzer constructs both
quotients directly and separates the shifted terminal row into even
and odd packets.  It certifies all nine nonempty even cutoff classes,
the full odd packet, and the combined payment in the six partial odd
classes.  The exhaustive stable-boundary partition has 906 finite
entries, 320 one-variable Newton rays, and 22 two-variable Newton
cones.  Exact reconstruction and vanishing ninth differences certify
the unbounded degree-eight polynomial identities; Q<=100 is an
independent recurrence audit.  The negative b=-2 band demonstrates
why the proof uses combined payment rather than a false standalone
odd-packet sign claim.

